{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>To the chief musician, for the sons of Korah.</b> For the sons of Korah: one of the sons of Heman, grandson of Samuel the prophet. R. Moses said: this psalm was spoken in Babylon. And some say: it speaks on behalf of the people of this exile." "<b>A maskil.</b> ומשכיל is lacking a root letter. Some say: it is a noun, like והודי נהפך עלי למשחית. In my opinion: the poem begins with משכיל."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:32.815943824Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}